Packaged app

The packaged macOS app bundles third-party packages. Two of them use the
GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later):

- eSpeak NG, through the espeakng-loader package. It supplies phonemes to Kokoro.
  https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng
  https://github.com/thewh1teagle/espeakng-loader
- phonemizer, which kokoro-onnx uses.
  https://github.com/bootphon/phonemizer

Because of these components, the packaged app as a whole is distributed under
the terms of GPL-3.0-or-later. The TalkToMe source code alone remains MIT.
licenses/GPL-3.0.txt contains the GPL text. The source code of each GPL
component is available at the links above. The source code of TalkToMe is
available from its public repository.

The build writes licenses/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt into the app. That file
lists every bundled Python package with its license text.

Models and services that the app downloads or uses at run time

The app does not bundle these files. It downloads them when the user selects them.

- Whisper speech models, converted by SYSTRAN for faster-whisper. MIT.
  https://huggingface.co/Systran
  https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper
- Kokoro-82M voice model and voices, through kokoro-onnx. The model uses
  Apache-2.0. kokoro-onnx uses MIT. The app downloads the ONNX conversion
  from the kokoro-onnx model-files-v1.1 release.
  https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M
  https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx/releases/tag/model-files-v1.1
  https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx
- Pipecat Smart Turn v3 turn-detection model. BSD-2-Clause.
  licenses/pipecat-smart-turn.txt contains its license.
  https://huggingface.co/pipecat-ai/smart-turn-v3
- ElevenLabs is an optional hosted service. Users supply their own API key.
  Its terms and data retention rules apply.
  https://elevenlabs.io/docs/api-reference/text-to-speech/convert
  https://elevenlabs.io/docs/api-reference/speech-to-text/convert

